-- title:
--   Second inequality in norm-class form, prime-power Galois degree
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $E$ be number fields with $E$ an extension of $k$ that is Galois, let $p$ be a prime, $m$ a natural number, and assume $\#\operatorname{Gal}(E/k) = p^m$, i.e. `Nat.card (E ≃ₐ[k] E)` equals $p^m$; let $\mathfrak f$ be an arbitrary ideal of $\mathcal O_k$. Work inside `coprimeToModulus k 𝔣`, the subgroup of the unit group of fractional ideals of $k$ consisting of those $I$ with $\operatorname{count}_v(I)=0$ for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_k$ dividing $\mathfrak f$. Two subgroups are restricted to it: first `narrowRaySubgroup k 𝔣`, the subgroup generated by the invertible fractional ideals of the form $(\alpha)$ with $\alpha \in \mathcal O_k$, $\alpha \neq 0$, $\alpha - 1 \in \mathfrak f$ and $\tau(\alpha) > 0$ for every real embedding $\tau : k \to \mathbb R$; second, the image of `coprimeToModulus E (𝔣.map (algebraMap (𝓞 k) (𝓞 E)))` under the homomorphism `raySymbolUnitsHom E` attached to the function sending a height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_E$ to `primeUnit k (w.under (𝓞 k))` raised to the power `inertiaDeg'` of $w$ over the prime of $\mathcal O_k$ below it — that is, $J \mapsto \prod_w (\mathfrak p_w)^{f_w \cdot \operatorname{count}_w(J)}$, a finite product over $w$, where $\mathfrak p_w$ is the prime of $k$ under $w$. The assertion is that the index in `coprimeToModulus k 𝔣` of the join of these two subgroups divides $\#\operatorname{Gal}(E/k)$.
--
--   This is the second inequality of class field theory in norm-class form, for Galois extensions whose group has prime-power order: the index of the narrow ray class group modulo the norms from $E$ is bounded by (indeed divides) the degree. It is used to obtain the corresponding statement for solvable Galois groups, [`M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut_of_isSolvable`](thm.html#M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut_of_isSolvable), the prime-degree case entering through [`NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_finrank_eq_prime`](thm.html#NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_finrank_eq_prime) and the induction through [`M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_mul_of_tower`](thm.html#M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_mul_of_tower).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aKummer_normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut_of_prime_pow.lean

import Definitions.Def_NarrowRayClassGroup

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open NumberField IsDedekindDomain Deep.NTSupply

theorem M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut_of_prime_pow
    (k E : Type*) [Field k] [NumberField k] [Field E] [NumberField E] [Algebra k E] [IsGalois k E]
    (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (m : ℕ) (hm : Nat.card (E ≃ₐ[k] E) = p ^ m) (𝔣 : Ideal (𝓞 k)) :
    ((narrowRaySubgroup k 𝔣).subgroupOf (coprimeToModulus k 𝔣) ⊔
      ((coprimeToModulus E (𝔣.map (algebraMap (𝓞 k) (𝓞 E)))).map
        (raySymbolUnitsHom E (fun w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E) =>
          primeUnit k (w.under (𝓞 k)) ^ ((w.under (𝓞 k)).asIdeal.inertiaDeg' w.asIdeal)))).subgroupOf
        (coprimeToModulus k 𝔣)).index ∣ Nat.card (E ≃ₐ[k] E) := by sorry
